[2m│[0m [1m[38;5;231mWhich task changes should actually generate a notification? (All are recorded in the log either way.)[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m [38;5;153mStatus / completion[39m
  [38;5;246mTask marked done, reopened, or moved between states. Usually the highest-signal event in a tracker.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [ ] Due date reached or passed
  [38;5;246mDue soon and overdue alerts. The only trigger that fires without anyone touching the task — needs a scheduler, not [39m
  [38;5;246mjust an event hook.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] Assignment changes
  [38;5;246mTask assigned to or away from someone. High-signal in multi-user, near-meaningless while single-user — but the field [39m
  [38;5;246mneeds to exist now either way.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] Title / description edits
  [38;5;246mContent of the task changed. Highest volume and lowest signal; common source of notification fatigue.[39m
